<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 25 December, from 336 to 1991.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">336 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,690 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The earliest recorded Christmas on 25 December</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Roman calendar compiled in 354 records the birth of Christ celebrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> on 25 December 336, the earliest evidence for the date. Why it was chosen remains debated.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/800">800 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Leo III crowns Charlemagne emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During Christmas Mass in St Peter's, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Leo III crowned</a> the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imperator-romanorum">Emperor of the Romans</a>. It revived a western imperial title unused since 476.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-leo-iii">Pope Leo III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">820 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,206 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Emperor Leo V is murdered in the Great Palace of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Followers of Michael II murdered the Byzantine emperor Leo V the Armenian in a church of the Great Palace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. Michael took the throne as the first ruler of the Amorian dynasty.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1000">1000 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,026 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Stephen I is crowned the first king of Hungary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Stephen I, son of Grand Prince Géza, was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esztergom">Esztergom</a> as the first king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, which became a Christian kingdom. The coronation is dated either 25 December 1000 or 1 January 1001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1025">1025 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,001 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mieszko II Lambert is crowned king of Poland at Gniezno</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-lambert">Mieszko II Lambert</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boleslaw-i-the-brave">Bolesław I the Brave</a>, was crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gniezno">Gniezno</a> Cathedral. His reign saw attacks by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus</a>, revolts by his brothers and the loss of the royal crown.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mieszko-ii-lambert">Mieszko II Lambert</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1046">1046 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">980 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Clement II crowns Henry III emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry III, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> since 1039, was crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-ii">Pope Clement II</a>, the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a>, whom Henry had made pope after the Synod of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sutri">Sutri</a> removed three rival claimants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Henry III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-clement-ii">Pope Clement II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William the Conqueror is crowned at Westminster</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a>. Norman soldiers, mistaking the congregation's acclamation for a riot, set fire to nearby houses.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington crosses the Delaware</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On Christmas night, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-washington">George Washington</a> led about 2,400 soldiers across the ice-choked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delaware-river">Delaware River</a>. At dawn they surprised the Hessian garrison at Trenton.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1991">1991 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">35 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mikhail Gorbachev resigns as Soviet president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a televised address, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-gorbachev">Mikhail Gorbachev</a> resigned. That evening the Soviet flag was lowered from the Kremlin and replaced by the Russian tricolour.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 25 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ernest I, Duke of Saxe-Gotha</span><span class="tp">1601–1675</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-vi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius VI</span><span class="tp">1717–1799</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muhammad-ali-jinnah.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Muhammad Ali Jinnah</span><span class="tp">1876–1948</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/atal-bihari-vajpayee"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Atal Bihari Vajpayee</span><span class="tp">1924–2018</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nawaz-sharif"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nawaz-sharif.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nawaz Sharif</span><span class="tp">b. 1949</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 25 December <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/makan-ibn-kaki"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Makan ibn Kaki</span><span class="tp">d. 940</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-de-valdivia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro de Valdivia</span><span class="tp">1497–1553</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francesc-macia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francesc-macia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francesc Macià</span><span class="tp">1859–1933</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/karel-capek"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/karel-capek.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Karel Čapek</span><span class="tp">1890–1938</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ismet-inonu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ismet-inonu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">İsmet İnönü</span><span class="tp">1884–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elena-ceausescu"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Elena Ceaușescu</span><span class="tp">1916–1989</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nicolae-ceausescu"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Nicolae Ceaușescu</span><span class="tp">1918–1989</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/carlos-andres-perez"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/carlos-andres-perez.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Carlos Andrés Pérez</span><span class="tp">1922–2010</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
